 "about": "A rule without an effect. Round 29 found that a customization may replace a rule by one without effect, and that the rule then no longer allows under DENY_UNLESS_PERMIT, where denying and not applying answer alike. Here the policy and the set are PERMIT_UNLESS_DENY: after the replace the check is false if the rule denies and true if it does not apply, and the filter tells a deny term, no term, an allow term and an empty condition apart, with and without a predicate. The last two cases upload a rule without the effect member (omitFields): the load golden says whether the PAP takes it.",
